[Result ""]
{<b>Exercise One — Third Hand High</b>

In each of the layouts in Exercise One, your partner (West) leads the 5, and
the 3 is played from dummy. Which card must you (East) play as third hand to
ensure that your side gets all of the tricks to which it is entitled?}
[BCFlags "600817"]

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "1-1"]
[West "Partner"]
[North "Dummy"]
[East "You"]
[South "Declarer"]
[Dealer "S"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal "S:QT9... KJ652... 73... A84..."]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{

<i>Play the ace, third hand high. You can then lead the suit back (the 8, highest
from remaining doubleton) and declarer’s queen is trapped. You end up with five
tricks in the suit at notrump. Playing low gives declarer an undeserved trick.</i>
}
[BCFlags "600818"]
[Play "W"]
S5 S3

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "1-2"]
[West "Partner"]
[North "Dummy"]
[East "You"]
[South "Declarer"]
[Dealer "S"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal "S:AJ4... QT65... 983... K72..."]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{

<i>Play the king — third hand high — to drive out declarer's ace. As long as you
lead the suit next to trap declarer’s jack the defense takes three tricks at
notrump. If partner leads the suit next, declarer will take a second trick.
Playing low gives declarer an undeserved trick with the jack.</i>}
[BCFlags "600818"]
[Play "W"]
S5 S3

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "1-3"]
[West "Partner"]
[North "Dummy"]
[East "You"]
[South "Declarer"]
[Dealer "S"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal "S:J42... Q975... A83... KT6..."]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{

<i>Play the king, as high a card as you can afford. If you play the 10, declarer
will win the trick with the jack and still have the ace left. When the king
wins, you can lead the 10 — highest of your remaining doubleton — trapping
declarer’s jack and establishing two more tricks for the defense at notrump.</i>}
[BCFlags "600818"]
[Play "W"]
S5 S3

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "spacer"]
[West ""]
[North ""]
[East ""]
[South ""]
[Dealer "N"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal ""]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{











 }
[BCFlags "17"]

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "2"]
[West ""]
[North ""]
[East ""]
[South ""]
[Dealer "N"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal ""]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{<b>Exercise Two — Only as High as Necessary</b>

In each of the layouts in Exercise Two, your partner (West) leads the 5, and
the 3 is played from dummy. Which card should you play as East? What do you
expect to happen?}
[BCFlags "600817"]

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "2-1"]
[West "Partner"]
[North "Dummy"]
[East "You"]
[South "Declarer"]
[Dealer "S"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal "S:... 5... A93... QJT..."]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{Play the 10, only as high as necessary. If South wins the trick with the king,
partner might suspect that you have the jack, and even the queen. Partner will
know for sure that you do not have the 9. If the 10 wins the trick, partner
will immediately know that you have the jack and the queen, since South could
have won the trick if South held one of those cards.}
[BCFlags "600818"]
[Hidden "S"]
[Play "W"]
S5 S3

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "2-2"]
[West "Partner"]
[North "Dummy"]
[East "You"]
[South "Declarer"]
[Dealer "S"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal "S:... 5... J83... KQT..."]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{Play the 10. Dummy’s jack is trapped and the 10 is as high a card as
necessary. If partner has the ace, the 10 will win the trick. If declarer has
the ace and wins the trick, your king and queen will have been promoted into
winners.}
[BCFlags "600818"]
[Hidden "S"]
[Play "W"]
S5 S3

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "2-3"]
[West "Partner"]
[North "Dummy"]
[East "You"]
[South "Declarer"]
[Dealer "S"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal "S:... 5... A63... KJT..."]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{Play the king. You must be careful not to automatically play the lower of the
touching cards, the 10. The priority is to play third hand high. You play the
lower of touching cards only when you have a choice. Here, if you don’t play
the king, declarer may win the trick with the queen, which may be singleton.}
[BCFlags "600818"]
[Hidden "S"]
[Play "W"]
S5 S3

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
