{<b>1-1)</b> <i>Play the ace, third hand high. You can then lead the suit back (the 8,
high from remaining doubleton) and South’s queen is trapped. You end up with
five tricks in the suit. Playing low gives South an undeserved trick.</i>}
[BCFlags "17"]

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "1-2"]
[West ""]
[North ""]
[East ""]
[South ""]
[Dealer "N"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal ""]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{<b>1-2)</b> <i>Play the king — third hand high — to drive out South's ace. As long as
you lead the suit next to trap South’s jack the defense takes three tricks. If
partner leads the suit next, South will take a second trick. Playing low gives
South an undeserved trick with the jack.</i>}
[BCFlags "17"]

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "1-3"]
[West ""]
