[East ""]
[South ""]
[Dealer "N"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal ""]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{<b>Exercise Four — When Partner Leads a High Card</b>

In each of the layouts in Exercise Four, your partner (West) leads the jack,
and the 4 is played from dummy. Which card should you (East) play on the first
trick? How should the defenders play the suit to get all of the tricks to which
they are entitled?}
[BCFlags "600817"]

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "4-1"]
[West "Partner"]
[North "Dummy"]
[East "You"]
[South "Declarer"]
[Dealer "S"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal "S:932... JT85... K74... AQ6..."]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{Play the 6 to let partner’s jack win the trick. Partner can lead the suit
again and dummy’s king remains trapped. The defenders take all of the tricks in
the suit.}
[BCFlags "600818"]
[Hidden ""]
[Play "W"]
SJ S4

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "4-2"]
[West "Partner"]
[North "Dummy"]
[East "You"]
[South "Declarer"]
[Dealer "S"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal "S:Q72... JT95... K84... A63..."]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{Play one of your low cards, the 6 to encourage partner to lead the suit again.
Even though you know declarer has the queen, you want to keep dummy’s king
trapped. Partner will have to lead the suit again in order to trap dummy’s
king.}
[BCFlags "600818"]
[Hidden ""]
[Play "W"]
SJ S4

[Event ""]
[Date ""]
[Board "4-3"]
[West "Partner"]
[North "Dummy"]
[East "You"]
[South "Declarer"]
[Dealer "S"]
[Vulnerable "None"]
[Deal "S:Q82... KJT9... 754... A63..."]
[Scoring ""]
[Declarer ""]
[Contract ""]
[Result ""]
{Play the ace to prevent declarer from taking\n
a trick with the queen. Then you must lead the suit back, trapping declarer’s
queen, in order to take all of the tricks in the suit.}
[BCFlags "600818"]
[Hidden ""]
[Play "W"]
SJ S4

