{<b>Key point.</b> The general guideline is for third hand to play high when partner
leads a low card. Before automatically contributing your highest card, however,
take a look at the card partner led and the cards in the dummy:

● You want to play a card no higher than necessary.

● You want to try to trap any high cards in the dummy.

● You also need to be careful not to block the suit by being left with the
highest card in the suit when partner is waiting to take the remaining winners.}
[BCFlags "600817"]

